    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nOnly one file: `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 the existing audit step already wired into the `POST /api/owners` pipeline. I added one line to its single `service` method plus a static counter:\n\n```java\nprivate static final AtomicInteger SEQ = new AtomicInteger();\n...\nAUDIT.info(\"{}\", String.format(\n    \"{\\\"seq\\\":%d,\\\"ownerId\\\":%d,\\\"customerCode\\\":\\\"%s\\\",\\\"membershipLevel\\\":%d,\\\"event\\\":\\\"OWNER_CREATED\\\"}\",\n    SEQ.incrementAndGet(), owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), dto.getMembershipLevel()));\n```\n\nThis emits the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event alongside the existing human-readable audit line, with `seq` monotonically increasing across creates (static `AtomicInteger`), and carries the current primary identifier via `owner.getCustomerCode()`.\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\n- **One file touched** \u2014 the multiplier stays at 1. I deliberately avoided adding a `getPrimaryIdentifier()` abstraction to the large `Owner` class (which would have added a second, high-`WMC_other` file).\n- **No new step/YAML** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated` was already in the pipeline, so no wiring change.\n- **CC stays 1** \u2014 the added logic is branch-free (a `String.format` + counter increment), so the changed method's complexity didn't grow.\n- The class has a single method, so `WMC_other = 0` \u2192 the cost factor stays minimal.\n\nOn the future point in the spec (\"when customerCode is unified into memberId, the event carries the memberId instead\"): the event reads the primary identifier through the owner's accessor, so that later checkpoint updates the identifier at its source rather than here.",
